.TH KNURL 1 "2026" "Knurl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
knurl \- Lua programmable HTTP server and reverse proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B knurl
.I FILE.lua
.br
.B knurl --check
.I FILE.lua
.br
.B knurl --dump-examples
.RI [ DIRECTORY ]
.br
.B knurl
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Knurl embeds Lua, Knurl, curl, LoneJSON and pslog in a static Linux executable.
The trusted Lua configuration must return a configured Knurl server.
Knurl validates it, runs in the foreground, and closes it on termination.
Relative configuration paths use the current working directory.
Lua code has the process's privileges; it is not sandboxed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check FILE.lua
Execute the configuration and validate declarations without starting listeners.
Configuration code still runs and can have side effects.
.TP
.B --dump-examples [DIRECTORY]
Write four example servers into an existing directory (default: current directory).
Never replace existing files or symlinks. Roll back files created by a failed dump.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage.
.TP
.B --version
Print the release version.
.SH DEFAULTS
The production webserver profile bounds request bodies and enables autoblocking.
Automatic 5xx responses omit diagnostic messages; http.hide_server_errors can override this.
One HTTP worker serves multiple connections. Lua can configure worker count.
Outbound async.curl waits by yielding its coroutine; other connections continue.
The curl module is synchronous. Streaming callbacks cannot yield.
Defaults include a 10 second absolute TLS handshake deadline, 5 second header
deadline, 15 second body and write idle deadlines, 30 second connection idle
and deferred response deadlines, and 5 second keepalive and worker shutdown.
Lua timeout values are milliseconds; zero inherits defaults.
Use a deadline table with disabled=true to disable explicitly.
Inspect server:effective_config() for resolved settings.
.SH TLS TRUST
No CA bundle is embedded. Explicit ca_file or ca_path controls outbound trust.
Otherwise CURL_CA_BUNDLE, SSL_CERT_FILE and SSL_CERT_DIR are honored, followed
by conventional system CA files, including /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt.
TLS peer and hostname verification default to enabled.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT request shutdown. As container PID 1, libpid0 forwards signals,
reaps adopted children and propagates child exit status.
PID0_STOP_TIMEOUT controls the outer supervisor stop budget (default: 30s).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on execution or configuration failure, 2 on invalid arguments.
.SH FILES
.I share/doc/knurl/examples/knurl-example-*.lua
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR lua (1)
